<figure class="essay-figure native-figure full-bleed evolution-visual">
  <div class="evolution-plate">
    <header>
      <span>Self-evolution</span>
      <strong>Experience must change the system.</strong>
    </header>

    <div class="loop-orbit" aria-label="Six-stage closed loop from environment through interaction, state, learning, evidence, and evolved capability">
      <details class="node environment"><summary><b>01</b><h3>Environment</h3></summary><p>People, agents, tools, institutions, and simulated worlds make consequences real.</p></details>
      <details class="node interaction"><summary><b>02</b><h3>Interaction</h3></summary><p>Reciprocal action produces trajectories that neither participant fully controls.</p></details>
      <details class="node state"><summary><b>03</b><h3>State</h3></summary><p>Explicit events and revisable latent state preserve what the interaction changed.</p></details>
      <details class="node learning"><summary><b>04</b><h3>Learning</h3></summary><p>Prediction error and correction identify which persistent component must update.</p></details>
      <details class="node gate"><summary><b>05</b><h3>Evidence gate</h3></summary><p>Held-out retesting asks whether the update caused improvement without reducing autonomy.</p></details>
      <details class="node evolved"><summary><b>06</b><h3>Evolved capability</h3></summary><p>A genuine update changes later prediction, planning, recovery, and transfer.</p></details>

      <div class="update-core" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><strong>Persistent<br />update</strong><span>verified change</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="causal-test"><strong>Interaction is data.</strong><span>Evolution is measured change.</span></div>
  </div>
</figure>

<style>
